---
import { Code } from "astro:components";
const steps = [
  {
    title: "Open the app. Nothing has been approved.",
    image: "01-start",
    text: "The empty screen is waiting for source data. Opening the app does not create a payment, approval or journal. The database file will keep your work when you quit.",
    alt: "Helix TUI empty state, with no payment and a ledger containing zero journals.",
  },
  {
    title: "Press d. Load the fictional £120 payment.",
    image: "02-demo",
    text: "The demo loads the invoices, bank event and suggested match. You should see GBP 12000, Payment INV-1, and a proposal for inv-1. Every displayed check passes, but Approval is still #0 and the ledger still has 0 journals. Valid means eligible for review; it does not mean approved.",
    alt: "Loaded demo showing the £120 payment, proposal for inv-1, passing checks and no approval or journal.",
  },
  {
    title: "Press a, type Osa, then press Enter.",
    image: "03-approval",
    text: "Now you are reviewing a specific proposal. The screen names its ID, invoice and fingerprint. Osa is a simulated reviewer name, not a login. Check the match, then press y to approve it. Press n or Esc to cancel. Approval alone still leaves the ledger unchanged.",
    alt: "Explicit approval confirmation naming proposal 1, inv-1, its full fingerprint and reviewer Osa.",
  },
  {
    title: "Press p. Confirm the separate posting step.",
    image: "05-post-confirm",
    text: "The app asks whether to post the approval. Press n if you want to practise cancelling: no journal is written. Press p again, then y when ready. The service checks the current records again before it writes anything financial.",
    alt: "Posting confirmation for approval 1 explaining that checks run again and settlement commits with the journal.",
  },
  {
    title: "Read the result. One balanced journal.",
    image: "06-posted",
    text: "The result shows debit Bank 12000 and credit Accounts Receivable 12000. The invoice is settled. The ledger has 1 journal, 1 settled invoice and 0 problems. Try p then y again: the same journal comes back. A repeated click must not record another £120.",
    alt: "Posted journal with Bank debit 12000, Accounts Receivable credit 12000, and one settled invoice.",
  },
  {
    title: "Press t. Follow the evidence.",
    image: "07-evidence",
    text: "The evidence view contains the stored source, proposals, approvals and journal. Scroll with the arrow keys. Press t to return to the summary, then q to quit. Start the same command again to see the saved result. Restarting the app does not reset the database.",
    alt: "Scrollable JSON evidence view from the real TUI, showing the payment and stored source delivery.",
  },
];
---

<section id="tui" class="chapter tui-walkthrough" aria-labelledby="tui-heading">
  <header class="chapter-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Try it first · about five minutes</p>
    <h2 id="tui-heading">Run it. Watch each decision happen.</h2>
    <p class="chapter-summary">
      The problem: reading the code is easier once you have seen what the code
      protects.
    </p>
  </header>
  <p>
    Imagine £120 has reached the bank. The app suggests invoice INV-1. Your job
    is to inspect that suggestion, approve exactly what you saw, then tell the
    service to record it. Follow these steps on your computer. You do not need
    an API key.
  </p>
  <h3>1. Open Terminal and check Go.</h3>
  <div class="command-code">
    <Code code="go version" lang="bash" theme="github-dark-high-contrast" />
  </div>
  <p>
    You need Go 1.23.2 or later, as declared in the project. If the command is
    missing, install Go from{" "}
    <a href="https://go.dev/doc/install" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      the official instructions
    </a>
    , then reopen Terminal.
  </p>
  <h3>2. Open your checkout.</h3>
  <p>On Osa’s Mac, the existing repository is here:</p>
  <div class="command-code">
    <Code
      code="cd ~/Developer/helix-recon"
      lang="bash"
      theme="github-dark-high-contrast"
    />
  </div>
  <p>
    On another computer, clone the repository first. A private repository
    requires access:
  </p>
  <div class="command-code">
    <Code
      code={
        "git clone https://github.com/glamboyosa/helix-recon.git\ncd helix-recon"
      }
      lang="bash"
      theme="github-dark-high-contrast"
    />
  </div>
  <h3>3. Download the dependencies and start a practice database.</h3>
  <div class="command-code">
    <Code
      code={"go mod download\ngo run ./cmd/recon tui -db recon-practice.db"}
      lang="bash"
      theme="github-dark-high-contrast"
    />
  </div>
  <p>
    The first build can take a moment. This command uses recon-practice.db in
    your current folder, keeping the practice run separate from the default
    recon.db. For a fresh run later, choose a different filename, such as
    recon-practice-2.db. Keep the same filename when testing restart recovery.
  </p>
  <p class="capture-note">
    These screenshots render the actual terminal output captured from Helix{" "}
    <a
      href="https://github.com/glamboyosa/helix-recon/tree/d8defc5a82eb0c0ae507eeb2cb131cec7d3a2f6e"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noreferrer"
    >
      d8defc5
    </a>{" "}
    on a 100-column × 32-row terminal, using only the fictional fixtures. They
    are not mockups. IDs and fingerprints may differ in a database that already
    has records. Tap an image to read it full size.
  </p>
  {steps.map((step, index) => (
    <section class="tui-step">
      <h3>
        {index + 4}. {step.title}
      </h3>
      <p>{step.text}</p>
      <figure>
        <a
          href={`/reconcile/${step.image}.png`}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          aria-label={`Open full-size screenshot: ${step.title} (new tab)`}
        >
          <img
            src={`/reconcile/${step.image}.png`}
            width="1920"
            height="1408"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt={step.alt}
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>{step.title} Actual captured app output.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
  ))}
  <h3>What to notice before reading the code</h3>
  <p>
    Loading the demo creates evidence and a suggestion. Approval records your
    decision about one proposal. Posting writes the accounting result. Those are
    three different moments. The chapters below explain why retries, changed
    suggestions and crashes cannot safely collapse them into one action.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the terminal is too small, widen it to at least 48 columns and 18 rows.
    If you see an existing posted journal, you reopened a saved database. To
    leave at any point, use Ctrl+C; q also exits outside the confirmation and
    reviewer forms.
  </p>
</section>
<style>
  .tui-walkthrough {
    margin: 56px 0;
    padding: 48px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #cbd3c8;
  }
  h2 {
    font:
      400 36px/1.2 Georgia,
      serif;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 30px 0 12px;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  p {
    line-height: 1.85;
    margin: 14px 0;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font:
      11px/1.6 ui-monospace,
      monospace;
    color: #5d6b61;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }
  .chapter-summary {
    color: #5d6b61;
  }
  .command-code {
    margin: 16px 0;
    overflow: auto;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #0a0c10;
  }
  .command-code :global(pre) {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 18px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .capture-note,
  figcaption {
    color: #5d6b61;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  figure {
    margin: 20px 0 36px;
  }
  figure a {
    display: block;
    min-height: 44px;
  }
  img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid #3b443d;
    background: #141818;
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #263e2e;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    h2 {
      font-size: 29px;
    }
    .tui-walkthrough {
      padding: 30px 0;
    }
  }
</style>
